# Review: SceneEngine

Re-reviewed after SPEC.mdl took on the View, Object and Tag model. The containers are built and well
tested: Group and Ungroup, library promotion, orphan pruning, the Views tree and isolation each have
controller or unit tests (F-9.9's guard included), and undo is the patch log the spec now describes, tested locally and through
plugin-canvas's `Apply`/`Patch` operations. Tags and container order are specified as planned and
are not built.

Of 103 items: 68 done, 14 untested, 10 partial, 8 diverged, 3 missing. Findings:

- **Tags and order are missing (F-9.6, F-9.7, `Tag`).** Layers still hide and order elements, and
  `layerOrder` sorts by layer before node `z`.
- **The older divergences stand.** F-3.7 (create size scales with zoom), F-5.1 / T-4 (read-only selects
  nothing), F-1.4 (`portalFrame` scales continuously) and the recomposed surface (Palette, Properties,
  Toolbar, GeometryField, PartEditor) still differ from the spec; the code has not changed since the
  previous review.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

